WEBVTT

01:30.230 --> 01:31.140
Careful!

01:47.200 --> 01:48.290
You're in my line of fire!

02:23.700 --> 02:27.370
The Continent of Cruzon. A place where oil isn't found in the land.

02:28.420 --> 02:34.130
People of the land are all born with a certain ability:

02:35.220 --> 02:37.990
The ability to freely control quartz.

02:39.720 --> 02:43.400
They refine quartz with high flexibility

02:43.400 --> 02:47.460
and create ligaments that can expand and contract at will.

02:49.940 --> 02:54.110
The ligaments control the movement of cams, make wheels spin,

02:54.110 --> 02:59.090
and push pistons for compressing air and firing bullets.

03:02.380 --> 03:06.820
People of varying strengths hold the power to control quartz.

03:07.840 --> 03:11.190
People refer to their ability as magic.

04:19.230 --> 04:20.150
Daddy?

04:21.640 --> 04:23.680
Aren't there any lighter ones?

04:24.130 --> 04:26.190
I'm sorry, Mr. Arrow.

04:26.190 --> 04:28.480
Even two year olds can levitate these.

04:29.940 --> 04:32.410
If he can't even do it as a five year old,

04:33.870 --> 04:34.930
then he's...

04:35.900 --> 04:37.710
an un-sorcerer.

04:59.380 --> 05:06.200
This world has

05:06.020 --> 05:13.040
nothing worth noting

05:13.200 --> 05:19.960
But we have plenty of love

05:20.070 --> 05:26.650
on our hands

05:26.820 --> 05:33.990
Those who

05:33.500 --> 05:40.660
have faith

05:40.410 --> 05:47.940
will act on behalf

05:47.350 --> 05:56.200
of their unwavering love

05:57.050 --> 06:04.560
If I could challenge fate,

06:04.090 --> 06:14.240
I'd act on all of my feelings

06:30.860 --> 06:35.490
Book One
The Time of Awakening

06:51.720 --> 06:53.140
Oh, hey Rygart.

06:53.760 --> 06:54.840
What are you up to?

06:56.090 --> 06:57.590
Hey, you—

06:57.590 --> 06:59.940
Get back here, asshole!

07:00.560 --> 07:03.050
I'll bring you back a nice souvenir from the capital!

07:04.170 --> 07:07.150
That idiot took off so he wouldn't have to help with the harvest.

07:08.180 --> 07:10.610
Not like there's anything good waiting for him.

07:37.450 --> 07:39.080
Rygart Arrow?

07:39.490 --> 07:41.500
King Hodr has summoned you.

07:42.890 --> 07:45.340
Water... W-Water...

07:49.410 --> 07:52.310
I didn't think I'd really find you collapsed here,

07:52.870 --> 07:54.950
but King Hodr was right.

07:58.080 --> 08:03.250
Well, I can't use anything that moves with magic.

08:03.860 --> 08:06.170
I'm sure that's how he figured I'd be around here.

08:06.170 --> 08:07.640
He's a clever guy.

08:11.090 --> 08:13.230
So it wasn't just a myth.

08:13.230 --> 08:14.990
You really can't use magic.

08:17.720 --> 08:19.210
Well, sorry about that.

08:19.210 --> 08:22.400
No, it's just you're the first one I've met in my life.

08:23.110 --> 08:25.230
I apologize if I offended you.

08:25.680 --> 08:27.360
Nah, I'm used to it.

08:27.360 --> 08:29.230
So, who are you?

08:29.750 --> 08:32.400
I'm Baldr, a general of the Krisna Kingdom.

08:32.400 --> 08:35.820
G-General? Oh...

08:36.600 --> 08:37.980
Go around it!

08:40.540 --> 08:41.870
Soldiers, get back!

08:50.190 --> 08:52.880
You Athens soldier. This is for—

09:01.990 --> 09:03.000
Just two shots?

09:03.680 --> 09:05.900
That's one enormous bullet.

09:10.110 --> 09:11.390
I can't reach.

09:11.390 --> 09:13.030
They're shooting from outside my range.

09:24.300 --> 09:26.430
Fall back! Retreat!

09:28.700 --> 09:29.960
Are you okay?

09:29.960 --> 09:31.440
Y-Yes.

09:31.440 --> 09:34.530
I'm sorry, Zess.

09:34.530 --> 09:35.800
Captain Zess!

09:37.480 --> 09:39.780
Cleo! Get up already.

09:39.780 --> 09:41.630
I was just about to!

09:43.460 --> 09:45.810
Lee, I landed it one of my shots!

09:46.030 --> 09:47.990
Landed on what?

09:47.990 --> 09:49.060
The enemies.

09:49.350 --> 09:51.340
You just got lucky.

09:52.850 --> 09:57.350
They only brought out three archaic Golems when we're a fair way into their kingdom.

09:58.450 --> 10:02.750
It wouldn't matter if they fought our nation head to head. We're five times as powerful.

10:02.750 --> 10:04.330
They wouldn't stand a chance.

10:04.810 --> 10:08.080
I'm sure they've focused their units
on their capital and the border wall.

10:12.630 --> 10:13.590
Let's go.

10:23.140 --> 10:24.920
The capital, Binonten!

10:25.690 --> 10:26.960
We're here!

10:32.020 --> 10:33.410
General Baldr!

10:33.410 --> 10:34.690
Welcome back.

10:34.900 --> 10:36.470
Thanks for keeping watch.

10:39.940 --> 10:42.880
Oh, you're really a general?

10:43.840 --> 10:45.110
Guess what, Mom?

10:45.110 --> 10:46.860
I was the best one in my class!

10:47.330 --> 10:48.500
Really?

10:53.300 --> 10:55.590
Listen up, this only costs 3000 yen!

10:57.630 --> 10:59.840
Rygart, is this your first time here?

11:00.040 --> 11:02.850
No, I came here once when I was a kid.

11:02.850 --> 11:05.100
My dad brought me.

11:21.160 --> 11:22.270
Ten minutes.

11:23.080 --> 11:26.670
It's too heavy for the low-rank Golem pilots who can't use a pressure gun.

11:27.600 --> 11:30.100
No, even for the high-rank pilots,

11:30.100 --> 11:32.830
I would say five sacks is their limit
before they lose control of their ligaments.

11:32.830 --> 11:36.530
We should modify the experimental
claymore to be wielded with two hands.

11:38.010 --> 11:39.270
Thank you for your help.

11:39.270 --> 11:40.460
O-Of course.

11:44.410 --> 11:45.610
Queen Sigyn.

11:45.610 --> 11:47.060
Queen Sigyn.

11:56.390 --> 11:57.400
Queen Sigyn.

11:58.960 --> 12:00.490
What should I do here?

12:00.490 --> 12:04.090
If you don't leave some space
open, it'll become difficult to—

12:04.880 --> 12:06.030
Queen Sigyn?

12:08.510 --> 12:09.750
Rygart Arrow.

12:11.030 --> 12:11.790
Si—

12:15.210 --> 12:16.870
Si-Sigyn.

12:18.550 --> 12:21.590
Why didn't you come to Hodr's and my wedding?

12:23.480 --> 12:26.350
I was... busy with some stuff.

12:28.580 --> 12:31.530
What's more important than your best friends' wedding?

12:31.530 --> 12:34.910
I could name lots of things! Like the harvest.

12:34.910 --> 12:37.610
So it's not that you don't like us?

12:37.610 --> 12:39.220
Of course it's not.

12:41.110 --> 12:42.370
Geez...

12:42.370 --> 12:44.910
I haven't seen you for four years and this is how you greet me?

12:48.840 --> 12:51.590
I'm so happy to see you, Rygart.

12:54.430 --> 12:56.760
Look at Queen Sigyn's smile!

12:56.760 --> 12:58.670
Who is that guy anyway?

12:58.670 --> 13:02.210
He's a friend of the King and Queen from back when they were students.

13:02.440 --> 13:08.300
He's one of those un-sorcerers
who's born once in a million years.

13:08.300 --> 13:11.380
I wonder how he's survived without using magic.

13:11.950 --> 13:16.290
What I want to know is why the King summoned him.

13:17.470 --> 13:20.510
Maybe he wants to reminisce on his past.

13:24.550 --> 13:27.960
King Hodr, I've brought Sir Rygart.

13:31.450 --> 13:32.280
Hey.

13:32.960 --> 13:34.100
Thanks for coming.

13:34.820 --> 13:36.620
Check out my chair.

13:37.290 --> 13:38.320
Hodr.

13:39.440 --> 13:43.550
As his wife and a citizen, what do you think about a king who doesn't like his throne?

13:43.710 --> 13:45.580
I heard you, citizen.

13:45.580 --> 13:48.510
For insulting the king, you'll pay with your life.

13:49.850 --> 13:54.500
I spent five whole days to get
here after reading your message,

13:54.500 --> 13:56.290
and that's how you treat me?

14:05.260 --> 14:07.400
Gram, you've gotten bigger.

14:07.400 --> 14:10.100
Thanks for coming, Rygart.

14:10.100 --> 14:14.020
Man, if you're gonna call me here, you should at least tell me why.

14:14.020 --> 14:19.770
Is the Troublemaker Quartet of Assam
Military School going to have a reunion?

14:20.190 --> 14:21.310
Troublemaker?

14:21.310 --> 14:21.920
Yep!

14:22.150 --> 14:27.170
A prince who was always looking at the sky
to lose some points and avoid the throne,

14:27.430 --> 14:29.300
a mad scientist who locked herself up in the school's lab

14:29.300 --> 14:32.280
for three days and nights, no
sleep, no food, no water, and—

14:32.280 --> 14:33.410
The King of Make-ups.

14:36.130 --> 14:39.140
Then Zess, who we call Mr. Uptight, completes the quartet.

14:39.140 --> 14:40.740
You called him here, too, right?

14:44.350 --> 14:45.470
Don't you know?

14:46.620 --> 14:50.070
One month ago, there was a coup d'etat in Assam.

14:52.990 --> 14:57.900
Athens and Orlando both made armed
interventions and it resulted in Athens' victory.

14:58.660 --> 15:01.930
Basically, Assam isn't neutral anymore.

15:02.300 --> 15:03.670
It belongs to the Athens.

15:04.990 --> 15:08.940
So the neighboring countries were at war and none of the news ever reached me.

15:08.940 --> 15:11.350
It's not simply a neighboring issue anymore.

15:12.170 --> 15:15.320
I haven't disclosed the news to the citizens yet, but...

15:17.870 --> 15:23.410
Our Krisnan Army and the Athens Commonwealth are already fighting at the city border.

15:23.810 --> 15:26.210
The defense of the Mizoram Stronghold is tough,

15:26.210 --> 15:30.750
but I've also received a report that a small platoon has broken through the grand canyon in the north.

15:34.590 --> 15:36.910
And the captain of that platoon is Zess.

15:37.990 --> 15:39.380
Zess?!

15:39.380 --> 15:41.460
No, that's impossible!

15:41.460 --> 15:46.200
I mean, I know he's from Athens, and he was also a prodigy pilot,

15:46.200 --> 15:48.510
but he hated war more than anyone!

15:51.020 --> 15:53.470
He enlisted to the army

15:53.700 --> 15:57.550
because he wanted to stop his brother
who's the Commander of Athens, right?

16:07.620 --> 16:10.320
The Mizoram Stronghold is holding out well, but...

16:11.060 --> 16:15.290
It's only a matter of time until they break through that too.

16:17.220 --> 16:18.080
What's up?

16:18.710 --> 16:20.910
Thanks for the valuable info.

16:20.910 --> 16:23.150
I'll be running away into the
mountains with my little brother

16:23.150 --> 16:25.930
before all of Krisna becomes a battlefield.

16:25.930 --> 16:27.090
Run away?

16:27.090 --> 16:28.400
You brainless coward!

16:28.400 --> 16:29.220
Silence!

16:29.810 --> 16:30.630
Sir...

16:31.480 --> 16:32.600
Hodr?

16:34.190 --> 16:37.100
Rygart, I need your help.

16:38.330 --> 16:39.760
You know my strength.

16:39.760 --> 16:41.770
I can't even fire a normal rifle.

16:42.150 --> 16:43.120
Come with me.

16:48.460 --> 16:49.580
Queen Sigyn.

16:50.150 --> 16:53.560
His Highness seems to trust him very much.

16:53.560 --> 16:54.790
May I know who he is?

16:54.790 --> 16:57.680
He is a friend from back when we were students.

16:58.390 --> 17:01.680
Well, he doesn't seem to be just any colleague.

17:03.300 --> 17:07.250
He's the only man who could stop a fight

17:07.250 --> 17:11.000
between the Commander of Athens'
brother and the prince of a kingdom.

17:13.250 --> 17:14.790
He's a rather odd person.

17:16.550 --> 17:17.930
An odd person?

17:19.360 --> 17:20.240
Yes.

17:22.030 --> 17:23.210
King Hodr!

17:23.210 --> 17:24.100
Your Highness!

17:25.230 --> 17:28.010
Rygart, is your father well?

17:28.010 --> 17:30.510
Oh, he passed away last year.

17:30.510 --> 17:31.360
What?!

17:31.360 --> 17:32.730
What about his funeral?

17:32.730 --> 17:34.320
Why didn't you invite me?

17:34.320 --> 17:35.970
We didn't have a funeral.

17:35.970 --> 17:37.360
No one would've come anyway.

17:37.900 --> 17:43.260
He raised two un-sorcerers and went into debt putting me through military school.

17:43.260 --> 17:45.370
He truly thought my power would awaken.

17:46.620 --> 17:48.120
A fool, if you ask me.

17:48.640 --> 17:51.380
I'd say he's an admirable father.

17:52.710 --> 17:54.860
He picked a fight with fate.

17:55.930 --> 17:56.960
I...

17:59.770 --> 18:00.930
couldn't.

18:35.940 --> 18:37.760
It's... a Golem, right?

18:39.240 --> 18:43.810
We dug this up last month when we were mining for quartz.

18:43.810 --> 18:46.060
We suspect it to be a millennium old.

18:46.560 --> 18:49.200
Under-Golem, you may call it.

18:50.610 --> 18:51.810
A millennium old?

18:57.980 --> 18:59.630
Distance to Binonten?

18:59.630 --> 19:00.780
About 1200.

19:01.630 --> 19:04.040
Sigyn's been really intrigued by this.

19:04.510 --> 19:06.290
That's why I called you here.

19:11.030 --> 19:13.390
It's the ancient who was in the Golem.

19:13.390 --> 19:17.800
Much to our surprise, that ancient doesn't have a trace of ever controlling quartz.

19:17.980 --> 19:22.300
Basically, this Golem doesn't mobilize with magic.

19:24.050 --> 19:29.580
I had several high-rank pilots try,
but not a single one could activate it.

19:30.900 --> 19:34.310
This is nothing more than a Golem mechanic's theory,

19:34.310 --> 19:37.500
but the ancients may have been unable to use magic

19:37.500 --> 19:41.560
and used a different method to pilot Golems.

19:42.620 --> 19:44.430
A different method?

19:45.050 --> 19:48.750
Rygart, can you help research this Golem?

19:48.960 --> 19:50.180
Me?

19:50.180 --> 19:55.400
If we can further analyze this Golem, we
may be able to strengthen our own Golems.

19:56.600 --> 19:58.210
Hey, Hodr.

19:58.210 --> 20:01.050
Are you really going to fight a war with Athens?

20:01.050 --> 20:03.080
You're no match for them.

20:03.080 --> 20:04.430
Let's surrender.

20:04.640 --> 20:06.520
I wouldn't say this in front of anyone else, but...

20:06.880 --> 20:08.810
I agree with the idea of surrendering.

20:11.020 --> 20:11.690
What was that?

20:14.960 --> 20:18.320
Athens has proposed a peace treaty.

20:18.580 --> 20:20.800
Then you can come in terms!

20:20.800 --> 20:22.020
Under the conditions

20:23.080 --> 20:26.580
of surrendering the entire territory to Athens

20:26.580 --> 20:29.480
and the divestment of all noble ranks...

20:31.460 --> 20:32.470
We're under attack!

20:32.470 --> 20:34.940
We're closing the border gate! Go back!

20:35.780 --> 20:37.370
Then let's surrender.

20:37.370 --> 20:38.630
Those conditions are nothing.

20:38.630 --> 20:44.180
You also used to say that it's ridiculous to choose a ruler through inheritance.

20:45.250 --> 20:46.230
And...

20:48.500 --> 20:50.390
Where are they firing from?

20:51.140 --> 20:52.580
What's going on?

20:57.710 --> 21:00.530
The execution of the Krisnan Royal Family.

21:02.670 --> 21:05.500
Sigyn wasn't born a royal, but it includes her too.

21:08.590 --> 21:12.650
In front of Sigyn and the Prime Minister, I must act as a king.

21:13.610 --> 21:15.750
Rygart, please tell me.

21:17.280 --> 21:18.250
What...

21:19.830 --> 21:21.100
should I do?

21:28.830 --> 21:31.510
They're firing from between two and five o'clock, at least 200 away.

21:31.510 --> 21:32.560
200?!

21:36.060 --> 21:38.240
They seem to have figured out our location.

21:38.240 --> 21:39.250
Okay.

21:39.250 --> 21:41.150
Cleo, go back to your Golem.

21:41.150 --> 21:42.270
Roger.

21:45.970 --> 21:51.190
They didn't write out the last condition.
They had their messenger tell me in person.

21:52.430 --> 21:53.770
Hats off to the Commander.

21:53.770 --> 21:57.560
Commander Loquis wants to take us over, not get on friendly terms.

22:01.670 --> 22:02.630
That's your problem!

22:02.900 --> 22:05.130
That's what Zess was always so pissed about!

22:05.130 --> 22:09.570
You act like it doesn't concern you even when your life is in danger!

22:09.570 --> 22:12.150
As if you've already given up!

22:12.630 --> 22:13.390
Sorry.

22:13.760 --> 22:15.040
Don't apologize.

22:15.450 --> 22:16.810
I'm not mad.

22:18.980 --> 22:23.730
In any case, we can't fulfill that stupid condition!

22:27.320 --> 22:29.610
Wait, that alarm...

22:29.610 --> 22:31.030
Your Majesty!

22:31.030 --> 22:32.650
We're under attack!

22:43.270 --> 22:44.260
Rygart!

22:44.260 --> 22:46.420
Your Majesty, are you okay?

22:46.420 --> 22:47.540
Rygart!

22:53.120 --> 22:54.970
Your Majesty, you must evacuate to the castle.

22:55.270 --> 22:56.270
But Rygart's—

22:57.050 --> 22:58.180
Go!

22:58.180 --> 22:59.770
You're the king for God's sake!

22:59.770 --> 23:00.310
Hurry it up!

23:01.140 --> 23:02.460
Please, hurry.

23:03.850 --> 23:05.860
Hang in there! We'll come right back to save you.

23:06.760 --> 23:08.810
Sure, thanks.

23:19.480 --> 23:20.790
You're such a pain.

23:28.930 --> 23:31.660
H-How do I open this thing?

23:37.540 --> 23:40.110
Is this... quartz?

23:40.110 --> 23:42.770
No, then it wouldn't respond to me.

23:44.010 --> 23:45.030
What the...

23:45.610 --> 23:46.440
Letters?

23:51.220 --> 23:52.410
Please, hold!

23:58.240 --> 23:59.920
There's more of you?

23:59.920 --> 24:02.710
Fine, I'll change into anti-human bullets.

24:10.480 --> 24:11.840
Are these hieroglyphs?

24:12.590 --> 24:15.550
The smaller letters resemble the language we use.

24:15.910 --> 24:19.520
New pilot re...

24:20.190 --> 24:22.420
Who am I kidding, I can't read this.

24:22.420 --> 24:24.090
Tregi...

24:26.350 --> 24:27.410
What the?

24:30.960 --> 24:32.630
What?

24:32.630 --> 24:33.740
What's going on?

24:37.880 --> 24:39.700
King of Krisna, Hodr!

24:39.890 --> 24:42.750
Zess, I have achieved our goal!

25:23.560 --> 25:24.160
Cleo.

25:24.380 --> 25:25.870
What's the enemy's response?

25:25.870 --> 25:27.610
There's no response.

25:40.900 --> 25:42.760
Is that a new model from Krisna?

25:51.060 --> 25:53.320
How high did that thing jump?

25:53.320 --> 25:54.110
Unbelievable...

26:02.860 --> 26:04.190
Rygart.

26:12.010 --> 26:14.000
Is that an Athenian Golem?

26:20.890 --> 26:22.610
How do I...

26:26.040 --> 26:29.600
You're pretty interesting, but this is goodbye!

26:36.180 --> 26:37.840
I moved the legs last time.

26:39.970 --> 26:41.740
Damn, I forgot to change the bullets back.

26:44.500 --> 26:45.840
It went back.

26:45.840 --> 26:48.610
It took a step back when I pulled the pedal.

26:50.800 --> 26:51.790
The pedal...

26:55.320 --> 26:56.550
Then I'll push it!

27:12.650 --> 27:13.850
Stay back!

27:57.290 --> 27:58.760
I'm alive.

28:00.860 --> 28:03.000
I hope it's not dead.

28:03.760 --> 28:05.050
Wait...

28:05.050 --> 28:06.850
If it's still alive,

28:06.850 --> 28:08.750
what do I do when it wakes up?

28:22.450 --> 28:23.750
How do I change direction?

28:29.310 --> 28:31.730
The upper levers control my upper body...

28:35.750 --> 28:37.670
How do I grab something?

28:43.500 --> 28:44.580
All right.

28:44.580 --> 28:46.660
Now I can hold them off for a...

28:46.660 --> 28:48.140
Yeah, right.

28:50.150 --> 28:51.190
What?

28:51.190 --> 28:52.290
You're still here?

28:52.610 --> 28:54.180
Hurry up and get out of here!

28:54.180 --> 28:57.420
And... go call for some backup.

29:04.580 --> 29:05.370
Your Highness!

29:33.620 --> 29:36.620
It's been a while, Hodr.

29:36.620 --> 29:39.540
No, King Krisna IX.

29:39.910 --> 29:40.880
Zess?

29:41.870 --> 29:43.880
I'll apprehend you.

29:44.530 --> 29:45.660
But before that...

29:45.660 --> 29:46.630
Wait, Zess!

29:46.940 --> 29:49.010
Rygart's inside that Golem!

29:51.080 --> 29:52.390
Rygart?

29:54.400 --> 29:56.520
Are you trying to buy time?

29:56.860 --> 29:59.370
He can't pilot a Golem.

30:01.520 --> 30:02.750
Zess?

30:02.750 --> 30:04.380
You're dropping out?!

30:04.380 --> 30:10.510
Rygart, it's already a miracle that you were promoted two ranks without using magic!

30:10.510 --> 30:15.430
If you quit now, you're just proving that the guys who ridiculed you were right!

30:18.560 --> 30:20.620
He just doesn't have enough money.

30:20.620 --> 30:21.540
Don't be so hard on him.

30:52.600 --> 30:53.450
Hodr.

30:53.810 --> 30:56.700
If I capture you, I can end this foolish war.

30:57.470 --> 31:02.750
I know you aren't the kind of man to joke, but there's no way Rygart would be here!

31:03.180 --> 31:03.960
Zess!

31:05.960 --> 31:07.420
Stop, Zess!

31:08.300 --> 31:09.540
We're moving out!

31:09.540 --> 31:10.300
Open the gate!

31:10.300 --> 31:11.790
General Baldr!

31:11.790 --> 31:14.810
Weren't we defending the wall to keep them out?

31:14.960 --> 31:18.720
Captain Sakura, I just learned that His Majesty

31:18.720 --> 31:22.270
headed to the mining site on the other side of the wall.

31:22.270 --> 31:23.060
What?!

31:27.340 --> 31:28.980
Zess! It's me!

31:29.890 --> 31:31.110
Damn, he can't hear me.

31:46.030 --> 31:47.100
Zess...

31:52.410 --> 31:53.850
Stop!

32:16.120 --> 32:17.160
Your Highness!

32:17.410 --> 32:18.680
General Baldr!

32:18.680 --> 32:20.500
Lower your body and aim!

32:23.120 --> 32:24.290
What is that movement?

32:27.620 --> 32:29.210
So he uses large caliber bullets.

32:29.770 --> 32:31.620
Angle your shield!

32:31.620 --> 32:33.220
It'll go through if you take a straight shot!

32:33.840 --> 32:36.220
Your Highness, it's great to see you're safe.

32:36.910 --> 32:38.390
Lee! Are you alive?

32:38.390 --> 32:39.440
Lee!

32:39.440 --> 32:40.220
Zess?

32:40.460 --> 32:43.160
Good. If you can move, then make your way back.

32:43.160 --> 32:44.230
Join up with Erekt.

32:47.230 --> 32:49.340
Zess, what about King Krisna?

32:49.340 --> 32:50.230
I failed.

32:51.980 --> 32:53.480
Walls of shields?

32:53.480 --> 32:54.240
We're retreating.

32:54.660 --> 32:56.680
This is a canyon.

32:56.680 --> 32:58.910
If they send their units behind us, we won't stand a chance.

33:02.720 --> 33:03.970
That crest...

33:03.970 --> 33:05.940
It's Baldr, the great general of Krisna.

33:05.940 --> 33:07.130
Lee, go now!

33:14.690 --> 33:17.150
We can't overwhelm them with this many units?

33:17.150 --> 33:19.600
So that's the infamous brother.

33:28.400 --> 33:30.130
The enemy is retreating!

33:30.490 --> 33:32.080
Don't make needless pursuit!

33:32.480 --> 33:34.360
The security of His Highness is our top priority!

33:44.360 --> 33:45.160
Zess!

33:49.250 --> 33:52.190
What the hell... are you doing?

34:09.350 --> 34:11.150
What an enormous bullet.

34:11.150 --> 34:14.020
We're taking this into Queen Sigyn's research hangar.

34:14.020 --> 34:15.730
We can't, there's no room in there.

34:15.730 --> 34:17.220
Then make some immediately.

34:25.880 --> 34:27.070
Rygart!

34:33.330 --> 34:36.160
Did you really fight in the Under-Golem?

34:36.160 --> 34:37.240
Are you hurt?

34:37.240 --> 34:38.430
Your eyes are okay?

34:39.470 --> 34:40.650
Yes, I'm fine!

34:40.650 --> 34:41.970
And you know...

34:42.590 --> 34:44.750
I moved that easily.

34:46.480 --> 34:48.090
You were researching it, right?

34:48.090 --> 34:49.640
Hodr told me.

34:49.640 --> 34:50.880
But how did you do it?

34:50.880 --> 34:51.960
With my hand.

34:52.820 --> 34:58.450
There's something like a small piece of
quartz in the front right part of the cockpit.

34:58.450 --> 34:59.740
About here.

34:59.740 --> 35:01.950
It just moved when I touched it.

35:05.560 --> 35:06.530
Rygart.

35:08.440 --> 35:09.750
Write me a report.

35:09.750 --> 35:10.840
'Scuse me?

35:10.840 --> 35:12.620
What you did and how.

35:12.620 --> 35:13.840
As soon as possible, thanks.

35:35.590 --> 35:36.710
Zess.

35:37.690 --> 35:39.860
I cooked dinner today.

35:39.860 --> 35:41.700
It's seafood again.

35:42.230 --> 35:43.670
Oh, thanks.

35:44.300 --> 35:44.910
Just leave it there.

35:45.070 --> 35:46.370
No can do!

35:46.370 --> 35:48.380
You didn't eat yesterday when I left it next—

35:49.070 --> 35:51.140
Don't disturb him, Cleo.

35:53.110 --> 35:55.710
Go relieve Argath from his scouting post.

35:56.130 --> 35:56.800
What?

35:56.800 --> 35:57.850
I'm doing it again?

35:57.850 --> 35:59.190
Why don't you do it?

35:59.190 --> 36:02.120
Oh, who said you could talk back to me?

36:02.120 --> 36:04.890
Isn't being continuously active the only thing you're good at?

36:07.680 --> 36:13.740
Argath and I need to do a check-up on our
Eltemus' for the second strike against Binonten.

36:13.740 --> 36:17.780
You don't even know how to adjust the
pressure output for the jumping mechanism.

36:18.400 --> 36:21.360
Right, Miss Zero Kills Cleo?

36:23.310 --> 36:27.370
I-I'm pretty useful too!

36:27.370 --> 36:28.410
Really?

36:28.410 --> 36:32.860
What are you proud of besides your breasts that're ridiculously large for a 12 year old?

36:32.860 --> 36:35.260
The bean dish with my grandma's recipe.

36:35.260 --> 36:36.790
It's delicious!

36:36.790 --> 36:37.380
So?

36:37.680 --> 36:40.270
I can... do laundry.

36:40.270 --> 36:41.210
So?

36:42.590 --> 36:44.400
Long-term Golem activity!

36:44.400 --> 36:46.890
I can pilot a Golem for hours without feeling tired.

36:46.890 --> 36:48.510
And that's exactly what I'm telling you to do!

36:49.200 --> 36:50.400
Fine!

36:55.370 --> 37:00.150
Is Cleo really the one and only
daughter of the Saburafu military family?

37:00.540 --> 37:01.600
Zess.

37:05.080 --> 37:06.390
I'm off.

37:06.390 --> 37:08.590
Argath, it's time to switch!

37:08.590 --> 37:09.540
Keep it down!

37:09.540 --> 37:10.840
You're scouting!

37:14.090 --> 37:16.000
Lee, what's wrong?

37:16.490 --> 37:18.320
U-Um...

37:18.320 --> 37:21.100
The new Golem I saw with Krisna...

37:21.100 --> 37:24.010
Its movement didn't exactly match its equipment.

37:24.190 --> 37:26.870
Oh, that odd one?

37:28.400 --> 37:30.260
I'm sure it's nothing we need to worry about.

37:51.550 --> 37:53.620
You'll die if you don't check properly!

37:53.620 --> 37:54.660
Yes, ma'am.

37:56.080 --> 37:57.160
Let's hurry.

37:57.160 --> 37:58.710
General True's waiting for us.

38:21.490 --> 38:22.360
Rygart.

38:22.360 --> 38:25.250
How long are you guys gonna work for?

38:26.780 --> 38:30.490
I can't do anything but sleep with the sun down, you know?

38:30.990 --> 38:34.500
We're polishing non-responsive
quartz to use as this Golem's armor.

38:36.250 --> 38:40.340
I thought you were disassembling it because it doesn't move anymore.

38:41.060 --> 38:44.880
We can't disassemble the inner frame from the outside beyond how it currently is.

38:45.060 --> 38:48.350
With our technology, we'd only be able to destroy it.

38:48.850 --> 38:49.640
Destroy it, huh?

38:50.310 --> 38:53.640
What technology did the ancients use to build this?

38:54.770 --> 38:56.640
It's so unbalanced...

39:03.250 --> 39:07.940
Unlike us, the ancients seem to have based their lives around metals

39:07.940 --> 39:10.840
which are well-suited with heat and oil.

39:10.840 --> 39:13.050
But for some reason,

39:13.050 --> 39:16.810
the inner-frame is constructed of quartz which isn't exactly fit for heat or oil.

39:17.520 --> 39:20.720
The exoskeleton was full of air bubbles due to corrosion,

39:20.720 --> 39:23.330
but the inner-frame isn't corroded at all.

39:23.800 --> 39:28.470
But if you assume they refined quartz using
inconceivable technology like the inner-frame,

39:28.470 --> 39:32.530
then their technology for refining
flexible quartz was rather primitive.

39:38.900 --> 39:44.500
It's as if it was created in a rush to fulfill one last duty.

39:45.780 --> 39:48.490
Earth to Sigyn.

39:51.470 --> 39:52.440
Rygart.

39:53.690 --> 39:55.420
Can you rewrite your report?

39:55.420 --> 39:57.000
Why?

39:57.000 --> 39:58.950
Because this isn't a proper report.

39:58.950 --> 39:59.790
What's wrong with it?

39:59.990 --> 40:01.970
It's a perfectly fine report!

40:01.970 --> 40:03.600
How so?

40:03.600 --> 40:04.660
Well, fine.

40:04.660 --> 40:06.800
I'll write, so can you explain to me?

40:07.520 --> 40:09.420
I put time into that...

40:09.420 --> 40:13.210
How did you crawl out of Mining Site 118?

40:14.380 --> 40:15.890
How did you get out of the hole?

40:16.340 --> 40:18.120
Oh, I jumped.

40:18.120 --> 40:19.780
Let's talk seriously.

40:19.780 --> 40:21.310
It was at least 20 mailes deep.

40:23.810 --> 40:27.480
You can't possibly jump that high without a run!

40:27.480 --> 40:32.150
Even the latest, lightest Golem from Athens can only jump 10 mailes!

40:32.150 --> 40:33.990
I'm serious!

40:33.990 --> 40:36.160
Ask Hodr or the other soldiers.

40:38.470 --> 40:40.160
So you're serious?

40:41.280 --> 40:42.160
Yes.

40:43.910 --> 40:45.800
What about the impact when you landed?

40:45.800 --> 40:47.140
Look...

40:47.140 --> 40:48.680
Just tell me how it felt.

40:48.680 --> 40:50.290
You're close.

40:50.290 --> 40:51.080
Close?

40:51.080 --> 40:54.200
See, if you could back up a little...

40:54.780 --> 40:58.180
I can't use magic, but I'm still a man, you know...

41:04.560 --> 41:06.690
Magic has nothing to do with this.

41:06.690 --> 41:08.420
Please redo the report.

41:08.420 --> 41:09.190
I don't need any drawings.

41:13.060 --> 41:14.350
Queen Sigyn.

41:14.350 --> 41:15.680
Is something wrong?

41:15.680 --> 41:17.200
Your cheeks are deep red.

41:18.260 --> 41:22.120
So this is the junk Golem that the ancients were using.

41:22.310 --> 41:23.700
General True!

41:23.700 --> 41:25.690
You're back?

41:26.270 --> 41:28.870
Yes, I just returned.

41:29.820 --> 41:33.840
Now that I'm here, Athens won't be doing as they please.

41:34.030 --> 41:36.840
We'll need more hangars than we could possibly have.

41:36.840 --> 41:38.770
This is junk, isn't it?

41:38.770 --> 41:40.760
Scrap it. It's taking up space.

41:40.760 --> 41:42.020
My...

41:42.020 --> 41:46.510
Yes, but Queen Sigyn is quite attached to it.

41:46.510 --> 41:49.070
Queen Sigyn, huh?

41:49.680 --> 41:51.270
Then it's out of my hands.

41:51.270 --> 41:51.900
Let's go!

41:51.900 --> 41:52.270
Yes, sir!

41:57.370 --> 41:59.620
It's like a useless blade.

42:00.110 --> 42:01.830
A broken blade, so to speak.

42:07.510 --> 42:10.130
You hear that? They're talking shit about you.

42:28.180 --> 42:29.650
Don't take it to heart though.

42:31.750 --> 42:35.020
It happened to my brother and I too.

42:44.040 --> 42:46.570
He can't pilot a Golem.

42:52.530 --> 42:53.250
Zess...

42:54.630 --> 42:56.580
You already retreated, right?

43:06.740 --> 43:07.770
Hodr...

43:11.620 --> 43:15.150
It doesn't look like there's anything I can do.

43:21.200 --> 43:22.020
Gram?

43:31.720 --> 43:33.130
Wh...What was that for?

44:04.910 --> 44:05.870
Zess...

44:08.470 --> 44:12.340
Krisna has around 200 Golems.

44:12.340 --> 44:15.750
More than half of them have been dispersed between all of their cities for defense.

44:17.890 --> 44:21.510
I'd say it's safe to assume that
around 80 Golems are in Binonten.

44:22.710 --> 44:26.510
Our intention is to destroy at least 20.

44:27.500 --> 44:29.140
If we can make them realize

44:29.140 --> 44:33.020
that we can annihilate a quarter of the capital guards with only five Golems...

44:37.970 --> 44:43.040
Hodr, as wise as you are, you'll definitely surrender.

45:20.790 --> 45:22.610
I already told you yesterday.

45:23.270 --> 45:26.290
I'd like to go over everything once more.

45:26.290 --> 45:27.310
Go over?

45:34.890 --> 45:35.710
Are they here?

45:42.580 --> 45:43.700
I-It's fast!

45:51.010 --> 45:54.480
We're engaged in battle at the northern gate.

45:52.630 --> 45:53.520
They're here?

45:53.520 --> 45:54.480
Looks like it.

45:55.190 --> 45:57.650
Damn, it's not responding at all.

45:57.650 --> 45:59.240
It was working yesterday.

45:59.240 --> 46:00.320
Rygart!

46:01.510 --> 46:02.450
Sigyn.

46:02.450 --> 46:03.790
What are you doing?

46:03.790 --> 46:04.860
I was explaining how it works.

46:05.240 --> 46:07.740
In any case, is Zess back?

46:09.050 --> 46:10.520
Yes, I think so.

46:14.270 --> 46:15.750
Why?

46:15.950 --> 46:16.870
West?

46:16.870 --> 46:18.330
I thought it was the north gate.

46:27.250 --> 46:28.820
Let me do it.

46:28.820 --> 46:30.010
H-Hey!

46:30.210 --> 46:31.220
Rygart!

46:32.000 --> 46:35.580
Hodr, do you think I can do something?

46:43.990 --> 46:45.150
It does move!

46:45.150 --> 46:46.380
What?

46:46.380 --> 46:48.110
Was it the glove?

46:46.910 --> 46:48.110
Sigyn!

46:48.890 --> 46:50.750
I want to talk with Zess.

46:50.750 --> 46:52.870
Can you ask the General to give me some time?

46:53.770 --> 46:56.640
I'll talk with Zess and make him fall back.

46:56.640 --> 46:59.040
I know he doesn't want this war.

47:00.750 --> 47:02.020
I'm borrowing this.

47:02.020 --> 47:02.960
Wait!

47:02.960 --> 47:03.460
Hey!

47:08.440 --> 47:09.370
Careful!

47:12.480 --> 47:13.310
As I thought...

47:18.200 --> 47:19.250
Queen Sigyn.

47:20.200 --> 47:21.250
Queen Sigyn!

47:21.950 --> 47:23.270
Get General Baldr!

47:24.020 --> 47:28.120
Yesterday, 30 minutes after Rygart walked away from that Golem, it lost its light.

47:28.650 --> 47:32.180
And it never responded to any of the pilots who tried beforehand.

47:32.180 --> 47:37.620
Could it be that we, who can use magic, aren't recognized as descendants?

48:03.440 --> 48:08.210
There is no one in the future

48:08.760 --> 48:13.440
Hearing voices only from behind,

48:13.900 --> 48:18.560
I look up to see wishes
blooming in the land

48:19.070 --> 48:23.820
I seek out the ones who
try to stomp on them

48:24.280 --> 48:31.480
because I never make
promises I cannot keep

48:31.770 --> 48:37.410
They're proud dreams,
so I'll make them shine brighter

48:37.410 --> 48:47.910
while bearing lonely strength
for the irreplaceable future

48:48.140 --> 48:52.360
"Don't just turn around
and move forward"

48:52.660 --> 48:58.220
You pointed me toward
the horizon I needed to follow

48:58.590 --> 49:02.760
I began to run and noticed too late

49:02.940 --> 49:08.190
that feelings die when they connect

49:08.540 --> 49:21.780
I will live in the present for
we may meet in the future

49:24.270 --> 49:34.250
Wind blows with no one in sight,
and I wander lost in this stronghold

49:34.670 --> 49:47.250
Even if there were others, I still
wouldn't wander into their wandering

49:47.490 --> 49:51.740
"Don't just turn around
and move forward"

49:52.010 --> 49:57.570
You pointed me toward
the horizon I needed to follow

49:57.910 --> 50:02.060
I began to run and noticed too late

50:02.330 --> 50:07.560
that feelings die when they connect

50:07.850 --> 50:19.990
I will live in the present for
we may meet in the future

50:20.510 --> 50:26.100
ALIVE SERIOUS AGE

50:20.510 --> 50:26.100
Alive in this serious age

50:44.260 --> 50:45.760
Preview

50:56.770 --> 51:00.240
The words the ancients went out of their way to carve...

51:00.420 --> 51:02.490
"Let us challenge fate."

51:09.660 --> 51:12.670
Book Two
The Split Path
